WEBVTT

00:16.010 --> 00:17.720
<i>In a distorted world,</i>

00:18.180 --> 00:20.810
<i>What can we do?</i>

00:19.020 --> 00:22.600
CONCERT OF THE DAY

00:23.810 --> 00:25.350
I'm turning off the AC.

00:29.480 --> 00:30.570
Alright, let's go.

00:30.740 --> 00:31.240
Got it.

00:33.740 --> 00:34.610
Starting the track.

00:49.840 --> 00:51.090
Are you kidding me?!

00:52.210 --> 00:56.640
Vocaloid songs are pretty
difficult to sing, huh?

00:56.890 --> 01:00.720
Your specialty is composing,

01:01.310 --> 01:04.640
So I really think we should find a vocalist
who's a good match for your tracks.

01:06.560 --> 01:08.520
I already said no, didn't I?

01:08.940 --> 01:09.980
I see.

01:10.900 --> 01:12.780
Well, can't be helped then.

01:13.190 --> 01:17.450
Let's just keep going with the two of us.

01:18.950 --> 01:21.040
I'm going to take out the trash.

01:21.830 --> 01:22.500
Rupa.

01:23.290 --> 01:23.870
Yes?

01:24.410 --> 01:26.790
Do you really think it'd be better that way?

01:27.580 --> 01:28.830
Here, take a look.

01:32.710 --> 01:34.300
22,738 FOLLOWERS

01:38.720 --> 01:41.180
If you really want to go <i>that far</i>,
it'll be a good start.

01:41.880 --> 01:45.850
AIM FOR THE BUDOKAN!

03:16.610 --> 03:20.910
ANTHEM OF THE
OUTCASTS

03:19.450 --> 03:20.910
So, how's your throat?

03:22.950 --> 03:24.830
It, uh, kinda got better.

03:24.990 --> 03:27.240
Like hell it did.

03:29.750 --> 03:33.580
Subaru, Nina, come to the sauna. It's good for your throat.

03:38.300 --> 03:41.760
Seriously...you're not gonna last long
if you're gonna be like this after every concert.

03:42.220 --> 03:43.010
She's right.

03:44.930 --> 03:45.890
Does it hurt?

03:46.470 --> 03:48.640
It's the good kind of pain.

03:49.140 --> 03:51.270
Really lets that post-concert feeling sink in.

03:51.850 --> 03:52.650
Owie...

03:53.810 --> 03:57.020
Either way, that was one mess of a concert.

03:57.400 --> 03:58.940
It was really fun though.

03:59.440 --> 04:01.320
And Nina <i>really</i> went wild there.

04:01.490 --> 04:03.530
You weren't exactly all
that docile either, you know.

04:03.780 --> 04:06.530
<i>And on drums, it's Pleia-chan!</i>

04:07.580 --> 04:09.200
<i>That's mee!</i>

04:12.830 --> 04:14.830
Well I can't exactly use my real name, can I?

04:15.290 --> 04:19.340
Gotta stay in character.
The super-cute JK, Pleia-chan!

04:20.550 --> 04:23.340
I, uh, think I'm gonna get out now...

04:29.140 --> 04:31.930
Man, she's completely hooked.

04:32.440 --> 04:33.890
- Who, Nina?
- Yeah.

04:34.600 --> 04:35.440
Is that bad?

04:36.150 --> 04:38.270
That's not what I'm saying.

04:39.940 --> 04:41.320
Momoka-san!

04:41.650 --> 04:42.400
What?

04:43.110 --> 04:45.490
I'm going to read you the comments from our concert's video.

04:46.200 --> 04:48.950
"It's not Diamond Dust without Momoka."

04:49.740 --> 04:53.210
"There's definitely more "rock" in her new group
than in the new Diamond Dust."

04:54.330 --> 04:57.080
Hey, someone said Nina's cute.

04:57.340 --> 04:58.540
Gee, thanks.

04:58.710 --> 05:02.970
Anyway, the audience definitely
prefers the old Diamond Dust.

05:05.220 --> 05:06.090
And?

05:07.180 --> 05:11.310
Are you going to ride that wave and start telling
everyone that the new Diamond Dust are fakes?

05:11.560 --> 05:15.100
That they should support us instead because we're more like the original?

05:15.900 --> 05:17.100
Is that bad?

05:17.270 --> 05:18.860
Are you seriously asking that?

05:19.020 --> 05:21.110
Did you see how much followers they have?

05:21.570 --> 05:22.490
Look them up.

05:24.400 --> 05:25.280
20,000.

05:25.530 --> 05:26.490
And it's going up.

05:26.660 --> 05:28.240
Remind me, how much do we have again?

05:29.030 --> 05:30.370
500…

05:30.740 --> 05:32.080
Exactly.

05:32.330 --> 05:34.410
Then what are we supposed to do?

05:34.580 --> 05:35.410
Nothing.

05:35.580 --> 05:36.580
Business as usual.

05:36.750 --> 05:41.000
Writing songs, rehearsals, and concerts from time to time.

05:41.300 --> 05:42.760
And then what?

05:44.420 --> 05:47.390
What's our goal?

05:47.930 --> 05:49.260
Aren't you going to college in the end?

05:49.680 --> 05:52.010
I'm asking what <i>your</i> goal is!

05:52.350 --> 05:53.720
You're annoying.

05:53.890 --> 05:57.970
I just got out of the bath, let me relax.

05:58.190 --> 06:00.560
But you know, I'm kinda curious too.

06:01.770 --> 06:04.570
I mean, you were a professional before.

06:05.110 --> 06:11.240
Why would someone like that suddenly
start a band with a bunch of amateurs like us?

06:11.450 --> 06:13.870
So I was wondering if you have
something specific you're aiming for.

06:14.410 --> 06:16.410
Not really.

06:16.580 --> 06:18.370
No general goals either?

06:18.830 --> 06:20.080
Nope, none.

06:21.460 --> 06:22.500
She's so annoying...

06:23.250 --> 06:25.510
Annoying, annoying, annoying!

06:26.010 --> 06:27.130
You got rice on your cheeks.

06:29.180 --> 06:30.090
What's up with her?!

06:30.260 --> 06:33.760
Every time I try to have a serious discussion
with her, she's always so, so-

06:34.180 --> 06:36.270
And you're way too aggressive.

06:38.890 --> 06:41.190
You're like a bull seeing red.

06:41.560 --> 06:42.360
Moo.

06:42.730 --> 06:45.480
There's no way she'll be honest
with us under that much pressure.

06:45.650 --> 06:47.490
Do you have a better idea?

06:47.650 --> 06:51.030
Slowly lead her into opening up.

06:51.200 --> 06:52.660
Slowly and carefully.

06:53.030 --> 06:53.870
That's called lying.

06:54.160 --> 06:55.660
No it's not!

06:58.750 --> 07:02.420
I wonder how she actually feels...

07:02.710 --> 07:06.800
Before that, what do <i>you</i> want to do?

07:07.260 --> 07:08.090
Well…

07:08.260 --> 07:10.260
To beat Diamond Dust?

07:11.060 --> 07:11.860
Yeah.

07:12.090 --> 07:13.850
That's one high hurdle.

07:14.010 --> 07:16.310
They're pros who already signed with a label.

07:17.060 --> 07:18.140
So, what are you going to do?

07:20.480 --> 07:21.940
I'm home...

07:29.320 --> 07:31.780
"Band goals"

07:33.820 --> 07:36.620
"Band how to become pros"

07:42.710 --> 07:44.590
- Becoming pros?
- Yeah.

07:44.960 --> 07:47.210
Eh, finally got the spark huh?

07:47.550 --> 07:50.930
It's not like we already
decided on it or anything...

07:51.180 --> 07:52.890
I just wanted more info.

07:53.340 --> 07:57.560
Back in my day, people from music labels used to
go around venues likes ours

07:57.720 --> 08:00.480
to scout people, ask them for demos
or invite them for auditions, stuff like that.

08:00.640 --> 08:04.730
But these days, they mostly just reach out to whoever gets popular on the Internet.

08:05.060 --> 08:07.730
Is getting signed by a label that important?

08:08.030 --> 08:09.240
Well, yeah.

08:09.440 --> 08:12.110
You can publish your music online,

08:12.410 --> 08:15.740
but you need labels for the
promotion and collab opportunies.

08:16.240 --> 08:20.000
Well, first you should get to where
Diamond Dust were in their indie days.

08:20.410 --> 08:24.540
They got almost 10,000 followers back then.

08:25.170 --> 08:27.380
That's how they got noticed.

08:28.170 --> 08:30.260
So it's about numbers after all.

08:30.420 --> 08:31.670
Pretty much.

08:31.840 --> 08:33.760
Followers are an indicator of a potential audience.

08:33.930 --> 08:36.510
The more you have, the more offers you'll get.

08:36.680 --> 08:37.510
471 FOLLOWERS

08:37.680 --> 08:39.160
Did... did it go down?

08:42.980 --> 08:46.020
<i>Watch the storm pass by</i>

08:46.270 --> 08:49.440
<i>The city is caught in a whirlwind of truth</i>

08:49.610 --> 08:52.570
<i>Where should we let it lead?</i>

08:52.740 --> 08:55.320
<i>If we can smile upon arrival</i>

08:55.490 --> 08:57.780
<i>Let us hold our hands</i>

08:57.950 --> 08:59.490
<i>It's not a dream</i>

09:00.290 --> 09:02.960
"If nothing's going to come of it anyway, we're better off the way we are now."

09:03.120 --> 09:06.080
"If we're going to get hurt,
we might as well just stay like this."

09:06.460 --> 09:09.550
I don't think you're completely wrong
to think that, you know.

09:10.000 --> 09:12.840
But you'll still have to change that.

09:13.420 --> 09:14.380
Otherwise, <i>that</i> sounds ridiculous.

09:17.300 --> 09:20.180
AIM FOR BUDOKAN!

09:17.800 --> 09:20.180
Do you really think it'll go well?

09:20.770 --> 09:22.560
I can't know that.

09:22.730 --> 09:25.980
Even the most compatible people
sometimes fight and drift apart,

09:26.400 --> 09:29.440
while others without anything in common
might just stay together for life.

09:31.730 --> 09:36.240
But something tells me you'll get
along pretty well with those three.

09:36.660 --> 09:37.450
And why's that?

09:38.120 --> 09:38.990
Gut feeling.

09:44.790 --> 09:46.710
Wanna keep going?

09:47.080 --> 09:49.590
We still have to clean up, so we probably won't have enough time.

09:49.750 --> 09:50.960
True.

09:51.630 --> 09:52.960
Nina, you okay with that?

09:54.670 --> 09:55.470
Nina?

09:55.630 --> 10:00.470
I wanted to ask if we could
discuss our stage outfits.

10:00.810 --> 10:02.220
I'm fine with that,

10:02.470 --> 10:04.810
But weren't you the one
who made them last time?

10:04.980 --> 10:10.230
Yeah, but I thought we could
go for something cuter next time.

10:10.690 --> 10:11.650
Something cuter?

10:11.980 --> 10:16.740
Oh, and by the way, can I pleease upload these photos of you to our socials?

10:17.990 --> 10:19.240
<i>Oooh, nice!</i>

10:20.450 --> 10:21.740
<i>Shining like a star!</i>

10:22.620 --> 10:24.620
This will definitely get us a ton of followers-

10:24.870 --> 10:26.330
ABSOLUTELY NOT!

10:26.500 --> 10:28.670
But you were so into it
when we were taking them...

10:28.830 --> 10:30.500
How about you post your own mug instead!

10:31.290 --> 10:35.010
Sorry, I just thought our fans
would appreciate some fanservice...

10:35.170 --> 10:37.380
And what if my grandma sees it, genius?

10:37.760 --> 10:39.640
Do you really want more followers that much?

10:40.010 --> 10:41.640
We need to be able to attract customers.

10:41.800 --> 10:45.390
In that case, let's all put on school uniforms

10:45.890 --> 10:48.890
and rebrand ourselves to
Shin-Kawasaki Girls' High.

10:49.940 --> 10:52.570
If Momoka-san wore a school uniform, it'd be like we're scamming people...

10:52.730 --> 10:53.980
Girl, that's a low blow.

10:54.150 --> 10:54.980
I'll kick your ass.

10:56.070 --> 10:58.400
But if that's actually going
to work, then maybe...

10:58.820 --> 11:00.870
Are you serious?

11:01.030 --> 11:05.290
Isn't that exactly what the new
Diamond Dust is doing?

11:05.950 --> 11:06.790
I know that.

11:07.250 --> 11:11.460
But we'll never even be on the same
playing field if we can't go professional.

11:11.630 --> 11:14.800
And for that we need a big audience, so...

11:15.250 --> 11:17.170
When did we even start talking so big?

11:17.420 --> 11:21.140
That's the only way we can beat them!

11:21.300 --> 11:23.930
And since when did we start
talking about beating anyone?

11:29.190 --> 11:30.350
I keep telling you,

11:30.520 --> 11:32.980
I'm not holding a grudge against them.

11:33.150 --> 11:35.070
I still don't want to lose to them.

11:35.520 --> 11:36.360
I don't care.

11:36.530 --> 11:40.450
Don't go shoving your daydreams
and personal circumstances on people.

11:41.700 --> 11:42.700
I get it.

11:43.120 --> 11:46.540
But I still don't want to lose to them.

11:55.710 --> 11:58.380
Listen, I understand you and everything, but-

11:58.760 --> 11:59.970
Good evening!

12:00.260 --> 12:02.470
But suddenly throwing this going
pro stuff at her is a bit...

12:03.050 --> 12:05.850
I don't think it'll be all smooth sailing
just because she already was a pro.

12:06.010 --> 12:08.520
And I don't think we can beat Diamond Dust as we are now.

12:08.770 --> 12:12.350
But I hate the idea of just giving up without trying.

12:12.690 --> 12:14.770
We're not in the wrong here.

12:16.320 --> 12:18.400
Medium without onions, please.

12:19.150 --> 12:20.780
Medium for me, please.

12:21.030 --> 12:22.570
Alright, two mediums and-

12:26.950 --> 12:27.620
Huh?

12:29.700 --> 12:30.620
Nice to meet you.

12:35.750 --> 12:37.920
So you were musicians.

12:38.500 --> 12:39.760
Allow us to introduce ourselves.

12:43.510 --> 12:47.050
I'm Rupa. And this is Tomo Ebizuka.

12:47.600 --> 12:49.810
We've been composing on
our own for a while now.

12:51.770 --> 12:53.060
I've seen this before.

12:53.230 --> 12:55.230
Yeah, it got pretty popular.

12:55.440 --> 12:59.570
So you two were behind it, huh.

12:59.860 --> 13:01.240
She's so cute...

13:01.490 --> 13:02.820
That's kind of you.

13:03.450 --> 13:05.110
Wait, so the reason you brought us here is...

13:05.410 --> 13:06.700
You want a band duel?

13:07.070 --> 13:07.700
Nope.

13:08.240 --> 13:09.830
- A complaint?
- Not at all.

13:10.160 --> 13:12.330
Ooooh, I know!
We're your 10,000th customers and-

13:12.500 --> 13:13.460
Wrong.

13:15.790 --> 13:17.250
You're pretty slow on the uptake.

13:17.500 --> 13:19.460
Scouting.

13:20.090 --> 13:21.880
- Is she talking about a-?
- Nope.

13:22.050 --> 13:23.720
S-c-o-u-t-i-n-g.

13:24.130 --> 13:25.220
Scouting?

13:25.380 --> 13:26.090
Who's scouting?

13:28.100 --> 13:28.850
Scouting who?

13:32.520 --> 13:34.020
Wait, are you stealing her?!

13:34.190 --> 13:35.060
No, dangit!

13:35.230 --> 13:38.770
We want all three of you to team up with us!

13:39.730 --> 13:41.230
- No way.
- That's right.

13:41.440 --> 13:43.740
We saw your concert.

13:44.280 --> 13:45.320
No way...

13:45.650 --> 13:50.740
So we talked about it a bit,
and thought it'd be a good match.

13:50.910 --> 13:52.370
No way!

13:53.290 --> 13:54.370
Girl, fix your record...

13:55.540 --> 13:58.420
But can't really bring in a big audience,

13:58.580 --> 14:00.800
and we don't have many followers...

14:01.300 --> 14:03.130
Same for us.

14:03.670 --> 14:05.010
We're in the same boat, huh?

14:05.300 --> 14:08.760
Though we did get offers from a few labels.

14:09.140 --> 14:10.100
Woah...

14:11.390 --> 14:13.390
But once we started discussing the details,

14:13.560 --> 14:18.020
we realized what they had in mind wasn't
exactly the kind of music we wanted to do.

14:18.310 --> 14:22.020
They just wanted us to make things
that would fill their pockets.

14:22.530 --> 14:24.360
That might be a bit harsh,
but that's the gist of it.

14:24.650 --> 14:27.780
Let's just say they weren't
a good match for Tomo-chan.

14:27.990 --> 14:29.700
And that's why you came to us?

14:29.870 --> 14:32.490
Yes. I saw your concert,
and it got me thinking.

14:32.790 --> 14:35.450
You guys definitely play exactly
what you want, just like us.

14:36.040 --> 14:38.290
So maybe we'll be able to you know, have a proper clash of opinions.

14:39.080 --> 14:39.920
You really think so?

14:40.170 --> 14:41.210
Am I wrong?

14:41.380 --> 14:43.880
No, that's exactly the
vibe we were going for.

14:44.050 --> 14:46.510
Nina's definitely an expert when
it comes to clashing opinions.

14:48.720 --> 14:51.430
- Come in.
- Thanks for having us.

14:52.100 --> 14:54.600
I'll turn on the lights in a second.

14:54.770 --> 14:55.640
'Kay.

14:56.310 --> 14:57.110
Was it here?...

14:57.240 --> 14:57.850
Ouch!

14:57.940 --> 14:59.350
Don't just go running around in the dark.

14:59.520 --> 15:01.440
Sorry...

15:01.610 --> 15:03.650
Huh? What's this?

15:05.530 --> 15:07.190
- A lizard!
- It's a gecko!

15:07.650 --> 15:10.200
So you're aiming for the Budokan, huh.

15:11.410 --> 15:12.410
Budokan?

15:12.780 --> 15:15.200
S-So what? Something wrong with that?

15:15.910 --> 15:17.710
Nothing at all.

15:18.000 --> 15:19.750
I think it's really cool.

15:20.210 --> 15:22.960
I never even thought of something like that.

15:23.380 --> 15:24.460
Same here.

15:27.840 --> 15:30.220
Say, how big is this Budokan?

15:30.470 --> 15:31.970
You don't know about it?

15:32.260 --> 15:36.220
Sure do, I heard about it. And saw it on TV.

15:36.560 --> 15:37.520
Country bumpkin...

15:37.680 --> 15:39.890
You're from Sendai yourself, you know...

15:40.560 --> 15:41.440
Wait, you're from Sendai?

15:41.600 --> 15:42.770
I'm from Kumamoto!

15:42.940 --> 15:45.110
Huh? I'm talking about the city in Miyagi.

15:42.940 --> 15:45.110
TL Note : There is another Sendai, which is a small village in the Kagoshima prefecture, deep in the countryside and much closer to Kumamoto where Nina is from. So basically Nina mistakenly thought they're fellow country bumpkins.

15:45.400 --> 15:46.400
Oh come on...

15:48.570 --> 15:51.740
Since we're close to it anyway,
want to go see it up close?

15:54.200 --> 15:57.620
Ugh, it's way too late for going out...

15:57.910 --> 16:01.120
Come on now, seeing your goal up close will be good for you.

16:03.290 --> 16:08.130
BUDOKAN

16:09.300 --> 16:10.630
If we manage to perform here someday...

16:13.930 --> 16:17.600
If we really do it, we'll prove that we weren't the ones in the wrong.

16:18.100 --> 16:20.770
That we haven't lost to Diamond Dust.

16:21.520 --> 16:22.350
I'm sure of it.

16:25.020 --> 16:28.650
Aim for the Budokan!

16:33.360 --> 16:34.910
So, what's the plan?

16:35.280 --> 16:36.660
I'll call Momoka-san!

16:38.040 --> 16:40.870
- Are you really that stupid?
- Huh?

16:41.080 --> 16:45.540
She's the one who said we should get a bassist and a keyboardist!

16:46.920 --> 16:48.710
But their goal is the Budokan.

16:48.880 --> 16:51.030
That's basically the same as going professional.

16:51.130 --> 16:53.430
Do you think Momoka-san will just go along with that?

16:53.680 --> 16:55.640
Fine, then what <i>should</i> we do?

16:55.800 --> 16:56.760
I don't know.

16:58.060 --> 17:00.100
I still want to talk to her.

17:00.270 --> 17:01.310
You're at it again.

17:02.310 --> 17:05.060
Is that the only way you can
think of, Miss Know-It-All?

17:05.230 --> 17:07.610
What other ways are there?

17:09.780 --> 17:10.360
What?

17:10.900 --> 17:11.650
You thought of something, didn't you.

17:12.190 --> 17:14.110
Promise not to call me a liar?

17:15.610 --> 17:18.450
I'll tell you, if you're not gonna
go "it's called lying" again.

17:23.660 --> 17:25.210
They're good.

17:26.000 --> 17:29.840
The mixing is well done, and the
transitions are impressive as well.

17:30.000 --> 17:30.710
I know, right?

17:31.010 --> 17:33.300
Anddd, they're a bassist and a keyboardist.

17:33.470 --> 17:36.840
Sounds like the perfect opportunity to me.

17:37.930 --> 17:38.850
What do you think?

17:39.260 --> 17:40.890
What did they say about it?

17:41.060 --> 17:44.020
They really really wanted-

17:44.390 --> 17:48.150
They'd like to try a session this Sunday.

17:48.440 --> 17:49.110
Can you make it?

17:49.440 --> 17:50.150
Probably.

17:50.320 --> 17:52.320
Great, then I'll keep you updated.

17:53.740 --> 17:55.860
- That's called lying!
- That's called going in with a plan!

17:56.110 --> 17:56.700
So, did she say yes?

17:56.860 --> 18:00.490
Well...not exactly, but she didn't say no.

18:00.660 --> 18:01.990
The heck does that mean?

18:02.330 --> 18:04.790
This is just how I see it, but

18:05.120 --> 18:07.750
I'd say Momoka-san has two halves.

18:08.460 --> 18:12.000
One half is fully absorbed in her music,

18:12.380 --> 18:14.300
giving it her all to create
something amazing of her own.

18:15.220 --> 18:18.510
She wants to see if her music
can resonate with the audience.

18:20.680 --> 18:24.230
But the other half is a full-on realist.

18:25.480 --> 18:28.480
She thinks of herself as having "dropped out
of the fight" when it comes to music.

18:29.150 --> 18:33.480
She wonders if there's even any point
to taking it seriously again.

18:33.820 --> 18:34.650
I see.

18:34.820 --> 18:36.360
That stuff doesn't matter to me.

18:36.700 --> 18:38.360
Is she going to play with us or not?

18:38.860 --> 18:39.740
I don't know.

18:40.320 --> 18:45.120
But I feel like she'll agree
if she likes our sound.

18:45.290 --> 18:47.750
She's a musician through
and through after all.

18:47.920 --> 18:48.960
I see.

18:50.380 --> 18:51.590
I think I understand now.

18:51.840 --> 18:54.050
So we have to start preparing now?
Sounds like a pain...

18:54.210 --> 18:55.510
Huh? What does she mean?

18:55.670 --> 18:58.180
Less questions, more doing as I say.

19:01.430 --> 19:02.390
A FEW DAYS LATER

19:06.520 --> 19:07.140
All ready?

19:08.640 --> 19:10.810
It feels good to play in a studio.

19:10.980 --> 19:13.570
Hey, there's something wrong with this cable-

19:15.610 --> 19:16.650
Wait, isn't that...

19:17.900 --> 19:19.660
What is this photo?

19:19.820 --> 19:21.030
Is it real?

19:21.370 --> 19:22.530
How did you take a picture with her?

19:23.240 --> 19:24.370
Don't tell me…

19:24.700 --> 19:25.330
Exactly.

19:25.490 --> 19:29.710
Tomo-chan watches every episode
at least three times while it's airing.

19:30.880 --> 19:32.670
She always cries at the ending.

19:32.880 --> 19:35.130
No one asked you for the details...

19:36.340 --> 19:39.180
Still, you're really lucky.

19:39.380 --> 19:43.050
Tendo Awa is known to prefer to keep
her distance from her admirers-

19:43.220 --> 19:43.760
Wait, <i>Awa?</i>

19:44.850 --> 19:45.390
That's me.

19:45.560 --> 19:48.520
- Details. Now.
- Yo.

19:49.890 --> 19:50.640
What's going on here?

19:51.060 --> 19:52.100
You're late.

19:52.270 --> 19:55.070
Nice to meet you. I'm Rupa, a bassist.

19:55.230 --> 19:57.110
And this is Tomo, on synth.

19:57.280 --> 19:58.690
Ah, you're the girls from the restaurant…

19:58.860 --> 20:00.990
Thank you for coming so often.

20:01.610 --> 20:04.530
Order something other than a medium
with a beer for once, will ya?

20:06.290 --> 20:08.540
Well, nice to meet you. I'm Kawaragi, a guitarist.

20:08.700 --> 20:11.670
And by that she means she's the great
Momoka Kawaragi of Diamond Dust!

20:11.830 --> 20:13.630
Don't think I forgot about you!

20:17.090 --> 20:18.630
So what are we playing?

20:18.880 --> 20:21.180
Can we do the song from our concert?

20:21.340 --> 20:23.590
I'm fine with that,
but can the new girls play it?

20:23.930 --> 20:28.220
Yes, we practiced a bit before you came.

20:28.640 --> 20:30.560
I'm gonna play it my way though.

20:31.020 --> 20:33.100
- Is that okay with you?
- Just a sec.

20:33.560 --> 20:35.730
Well, we won't know if we don't try.

20:36.150 --> 20:37.110
Agreed.

20:38.230 --> 20:39.860
Alright, I'm ready.

20:41.400 --> 20:42.990
<i>One, two, three, four.</i>

20:50.620 --> 20:51.620
<i>Amazing.</i>

20:51.620 --> 20:52.620
<i>It's insane.</i>

20:52.620 --> 20:53.620
<i>Wow…</i>

20:56.790 --> 20:59.840
<i>The city is caught in a whirlwind of truth</i>

21:00.010 --> 21:03.090
<i>Where should we let it lead?</i>

21:03.260 --> 21:05.850
<i>In a distorted world</i>

21:06.010 --> 21:10.390
<i>What can we do?</i>

21:20.320 --> 21:21.990
Momoka-san.

21:23.030 --> 21:27.530
We were wondering if
they could join the band.

21:29.160 --> 21:31.120
I really want to give it a shot.

21:31.540 --> 21:33.210
I want to prove that you aren't in the wrong.

21:33.790 --> 21:35.880
That your songs won't lose to theirs.

21:36.420 --> 21:37.840
I want to show them!

21:43.340 --> 21:44.010
A festival?

21:44.180 --> 21:47.050
The first step is to get noticed there.

21:47.430 --> 21:49.930
They have an amateur division.

21:50.100 --> 21:54.060
We send in a demo, we get selected to play,
we go on stage, and get attention. That's the plan.

21:54.270 --> 21:57.020
And then we get offers from music labels?

21:57.400 --> 21:57.980
Yes.

21:59.070 --> 22:02.530
Well, festivals are the playground of producers.

22:02.690 --> 22:04.650
So they'll definitely be on the lookout.

22:04.900 --> 22:07.280
Hoping to find a diamond in the rough.

22:07.740 --> 22:08.700
So there we'll-

22:10.660 --> 22:12.040
Diamond Dust.

22:26.430 --> 22:28.890
Nina Iseri: Rina Momoka Kawaragi: Yûri

22:30.510 --> 22:33.890
Subaru Awa: Mirei

22:34.930 --> 22:38.310
Rupa: Shuri Tomo Ebizuka: Natsu

23:42.040 --> 23:45.050
Translation & Subtitling: JSICMF Proofreading: Sarah Courchay

23:47.170 --> 23:49.050
<i>To be continued: "Finding a name".</i>
